WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:03.489
Speaker 1: s coming out of the House of Representatives.

00:00:03.489 --> 00:00:09.530
Nancy Pelosi now says that the House of Representatives
is indeed going to move forward on an assault

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.650
weapons ban.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.889
There was previously an assault weapons ban
that ran from 1994 to 2004 in the United States.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:17.820
And we will talk about that in a moment.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.140
Speaker of the House Nancy Pelosi says House
Democrats will soon consider legislation banning

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:27.029
military style, quote, assault weapons, marking
the most aggressive response from Congress

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:32.140
to date following last week's shooting massacre
at a Texas elementary school.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:37.050
House Democratic leaders have already scheduled
to vote next week on so-called red flag legislation

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.080
designed to keep weapons from potentially
violent people.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.320
The House Judiciary Committee is meeting in
an emergency session to mark up a slate of

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.280
eight additional anti-gun violence bills,
including proposals to ban high capacity magazines

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.820
and raise the age for purchasing certain semiautomatic
rifles.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.331
I am in favor of all of this and also recognize
that it is not enough, and we're going to

00:00:57.331 --> 00:00:58.440
get back to that.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:04.280
Now, on the question of whether mass shootings
went down during the assault weapons ban and

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.620
then went back up after it has been examined
by PolitiFact and it has been found to be

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:09.620
mostly true.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:14.330
Joe Biden said when we passed the assault
weapons ban, mass shootings went down.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.750
When the law expired, mass shootings tripled.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.970
PolitiFact has ruled that is mostly true.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.630
There explanation is let me find it here.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.490
There are numbers that back Biden up.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:32.630
A 2019 study out of NYU School of Medicine
found mass shooting deaths involving assault

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:38.020
weapons fell slightly in the decade of the
federal assault weapon ban and then rose dramatically

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.050
in the decade that followed.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:44.421
While other researchers said the decline was
too small to draw firm conclusions, there's

00:01:44.421 --> 00:01:50.060
no debate that the pace and deadliness of
shootings went up after the ban ended.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:55.490
Beyond assault weapons, more recent work points
to the threat posed by large capacity magazines,

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:58.060
which the 1994 law also restricted.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:03.130
That is also a factor with the same guns but
without the large capacity magazines.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.160
You would also see less, less death.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:12.560
So if you go back to last week, I had my segment
where I laid out it was either ten or 11 specific

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.170
ideas on gun safety.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:20.650
And in that list I included limiting certain
firearms to 25 plus some.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:27.420
Some are saying 21 plus I say 25 plus requiring
mandatory gun insurance, requiring more extensive

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.480
training and relicensing a mandatory waiting
period of, of course, reducing the ability

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:39.370
to have the high capacity magazines, a mandatory
initial and periodic mental health evaluations

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:45.490
requiring 2 to 3 letters from adults in the
community, saying, I have no concerns about

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.190
this individual under age 25 having firearms.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:51.380
I gave a long list, but we actually need to
do more than that.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.560
And of course, Republicans are going to oppose
this.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:59.630
I say that Democrats, in conjunction with
this bill to ban assault weapons again, which

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.410
will it pass in the Senate?

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.430
Rob Probably not.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:09.240
Quite frankly, unfortunately, they should
call the bluff of the Republicans saying,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.790
well, this is a mental health issue, proposed
mental health legislation as well.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:20.340
Now, of course, part of that is red flag laws,
which would prevent individuals flagged for

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:26.459
concerning behavior and diagnoses from it,
would prevent them from getting weapons.

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:33.880
But do something more significant require
require an initial mental health eval as well

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.380
as periodic ones.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.090
Now, I know a lot of people have raised the
question.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.980
Let's say you do that, David.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.090
What are you looking for?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:48.310
Is it just a psychiatrist meets with everybody
and then evaluates for what what conditions

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.870
prevent you from getting a gun?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:55.660
How does anxiety compare with borderline personality
disorder compare with if you've had a psychotic

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:56.660
episode?

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.120
Well, you've got to figure that out.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.989
The fact that it's complicated can't be a
reason not to do it.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:07.209
I concede it's complicated, but it absolutely
needs to be done.

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:11.890
If all of these things were in place when
it came to the shooter in Texas, can't buy

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:15.270
the weapons he bought because he's under age
25.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:18.379
Even to get a handgun needs to have letters
from the community.

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:23.219
Supposedly members in the community were already
some were already concerned about this individual.

00:04:23.219 --> 00:04:29.439
Limits on high capacity magazines waiting
period, mandatory insurance which would have

00:04:29.439 --> 00:04:33.259
made it more expensive and maybe dissuaded,
although he reportedly spent a bunch of money

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:34.599
on the guns.

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:41.039
Those things at least had the chance, the
chance of impacting that individual's ability

00:04:41.039 --> 00:04:46.380
to get those firearms and those bullets and
to kill as many people.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:51.360
Could he have ended up killing five with a
couple of handguns?

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.169
Yes, absolutely.

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:58.860
But as tragic as those five deaths would be,
would we prefer five instead of 20?

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.009
I mean, I would I would.

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:08.099
So I would like to see Democrats not only
push for the assault weapons ban, propose

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:13.389
some mental health legislation to Republicans,
including increased funding as well.

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:14.979
At the state level, they don't want it.

00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:19.300
Many states didn't even do the Medicare the
Medicaid expansion that was part of Obamacare,

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.909
which would have increased access as well.

00:05:20.909 --> 00:05:25.639
So make them put up or shut up, make them
go on record as opposing the mental health

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:26.639
legislation.

00:05:26.639 --> 00:05:28.539
They're the ones claiming that's the first
thing to look at.

00:05:28.539 --> 00:05:29.599
Well, look at it.

00:05:29.599 --> 00:05:30.629
But also look at guns.

00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:32.439
And we've got to look at a lot of other things.

